##
## Upstream tests to disable
##
## When adding a new filter to this list, please include a short description of
## why the filter is required and create an associated tracking issue.
##

# These upstream Chromium tests abort in ~BrowserTaskEnvironment with
# "Check failed: MainThreadIsIdle()" and a single pending UI task posted from
# dbus::ObjectProxy::OnPendingCallIsComplete; the test bodies themselves pass.
# A shared D-Bus bus is a process-wide lazy singleton
# (components/dbus/thread_linux/dbus_thread_linux.cc) that captures
# SequencedTaskRunner::GetCurrentDefault() as its origin task runner when it is
# first constructed (dbus/bus.cc:186), so replies go to the task runner of
# whichever test first created the bus, i.e. to that test's own
# BrowserTaskEnvironment queue. ~BrowserTaskEnvironment runs RunUntilIdle()
# before the CHECK at content/public/test/browser_task_environment.cc:151 (the
# line named in every crash log), so this is not a merely undrained queue: the
# reply comes from the D-Bus thread and can land after that drain. That is why
# the abort is intermittent and depends on test ordering.
# No test body is implicated: the five reported methods are the four
# GetExpirationDescription* tests, which only format a timestamp, plus
# CreateChooserExceptionObject, which shares nothing with them, and all five
# abort identically at teardown with the same single pending task. The D-Bus
# caller was not identified - neither BrowserTaskEnvironment nor
# SetUpGlobalFeaturesForTesting issues a D-Bus call itself - so the shared bus
# is reached from elsewhere in the unit_tests process. Every method of the
# fixture is therefore equally exposed, which is why the whole fixture is
# filtered instead of just the methods reported so far: for example
# GetExpirationDescription_Tomorrow_LessThan24_AfterMidnight differs from the
# reported _BeforeMidnight sibling only by the offset it passes in and the
# plural count it expects.
# Every report comes from brave-browser-build-linux-x64-ubsan and none from any
# other builder, hence the ubsan-only filter; the fixture stays enabled
# everywhere else.
# Upstream flake data: LUCI Analysis reports STABLE UPSTREAM at a flake rate of
# 0.1% or less over a 60 day lookback for the SiteSettingsHelperTest methods,
# queried one at a time because script/check-upstream-flake.py truncates a
# suite-wide query to five test IDs. That is expected for an abort that depends
# on which test runs first in a test launcher batch rather than on the test
# body.
# Brave code is not implicated in the D-Bus call: no code under src/brave
# constructs a dbus::Bus or calls dbus_thread_linux::GetSharedSessionBus(), and
# the two Brave changes that do sit in session bus code paths cannot post this
# task - patches/components-os_crypt-async-browser-freedesktop_secret_key_
# provider.h.patch only renames string constants, and
# chromium_src/services/device/geolocation/location_provider_linux_portal.cc
# removes a session bus user by returning nullptr from
# NewSystemLocationProvider(). patches/chrome-browser-global_features.cc.patch
# does route GlobalFeatures::CreateGlobalFeatures() through BraveGlobalFeatures,
# but that constructor only creates ExtensionMalwareBlocklist behind the
# disabled-by-default kExtensionMalwareBlocklist feature. Finally
# patches/chrome-browser-ui-webui-settings-site_settings_helper.cc.patch, the
# matching .h patch and
# chromium_src/chrome/browser/ui/webui/settings/site_settings_helper.cc only
# add Brave content settings types, an "autoplay" group name special case, a
# Brave cookie type field, a SiteSettingSource value and _ChromiumImpl renames
# of three functions - all synchronous, none of it posts tasks.
# https://github.com/brave/brave-browser/issues/58316
# https://github.com/brave/brave-browser/issues/58352
# https://github.com/brave/brave-browser/issues/58367
# https://github.com/brave/brave-browser/issues/58465
# https://github.com/brave/brave-browser/issues/58538
-SiteSettingsHelperTest.*
